# striim-testing-framework-utility settings.
#
# Copy this file to .env in the clone root (`cp .env.example .env`) and fill it in.
# Lines are KEY=value. Quotes, an `export ` prefix and trailing ` # comments` are allowed.
# A variable already set in your shell wins over the same key here.
# A relative path here is resolved against this file's directory.
# `striim-test doctor` checks this file and names anything wrong in it.
# Every setting, where it can be set and its default: docs/SETTINGS.md.

# --- Striim target -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Your own Striim server: its root URL (no path), and a user allowed to create and drop
# apps. Leave STRIIM_URL unset to run in Docker mode instead: the first run downloads the
# Striim packages, builds a Striim image and starts a cluster (see docs/RUN-YOUR-FIRST-TEST.md, "Docker mode").
# Docker mode on a machine with more than 12 CPUs: the license caps the CPUs the cluster counts
# (24 in the tested licenses), and each of its two nodes counts every CPU it sees. Cap both in
# your shell, not here, so they add up to the cap (docs/RUN-YOUR-FIRST-TEST.md):
#   export SLT_STRIIM_PRIMARY_CPUS=12 SLT_STRIIM_NODE_CPUS=12
# Docker mode when you already have the Striim installers: skip the first run's 6.3 GB download by
# exporting a manifest of them, in your shell, not here (docs/RUN-YOUR-FIRST-TEST.md has the format):
#   export SLT_STRIIM_DEPS_MANIFEST=/path/to/deps-manifest.json
# STRIIM_URL=http://striim.example.com:9080
# STRIIM_USER=admin
# STRIIM_PASS=
# Default timeout on Striim REST calls, seconds: "600" (read), "10,600" (connect,read), or "0" for none.
# The login and read-only polls (status, MON, DESCRIBE, SHOW ... CHECKPOINT HISTORY, LIST LIBRARIES,
# LIST DEPLOYMENTGROUPS) use (10,120), re-login the rest of its deadline; "0" also turns these off.
# Jar LOAD/UNLOAD use none.
# STRIIM_API_TIMEOUT=10,600

# --- Infrastructure ownership --------------------------------------------------------------
# Every live run must say whether it owns the Striim cluster and the service containers it
# uses; a run with SLT_INFRA_OWNERSHIP unset is refused before it starts anything.
# `shared` (the default here): reuse whatever is already running, start what is missing, and
# never tear any of it down. SLT_KEEP_SERVICES=1 is required with it. Safe on a cluster that
# other people use.
# `exclusive` (opt-in): the run takes a fresh stack of its own, refuses to start if a Striim
# already answers on the endpoint, and tears everything down at the end (remove
# SLT_KEEP_SERVICES=1 for that). Set it only on a machine where nothing else uses that endpoint.
SLT_INFRA_OWNERSHIP=shared
SLT_KEEP_SERVICES=1

# --- Case locations ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the live cases are. `striim-test run PATH` only runs cases under this folder, so it
# must cover the samples (samples/live and samples/code). Several roots: separate them with `:`.
SLT_LIVE_CASES=samples
# The project root: case IDs are relative to it. Default: this clone. Setting it here does
# not move this .env file, which is read from the root given in the shell, or from the clone.
# `example:` and `jar:` paths in a test.yaml: see docs/TESTING-YOUR-JAVA.md.
# SLT_PROJECT_ROOT=
# Integration cases (`test.yaml` without TQL, run by the inttest engine). None ship with this
# repo; set this to your own.
# SLT_INT_CASES=
# Where run directories and coordination files are written. Default: scripts/live.
# SLT_STATE_DIR=

# --- Optional services ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# A case lists the databases it needs under `requires:` in its test.yaml. The samples need
# Postgres. Each required service (Postgres, Oracle, MySQL, SQL Server, Vertica, Kafka, GCS
# and Spanner emulators) is started in Docker by the run, with test-only credentials, and nothing
# needs to be set here for that. docs/SERVICES.md lists every account, port and URL.
# To use your own database instead, set its host here (or export it: the shell wins). The
# other settings default to the Docker values. For Postgres (docs/SERVICES.md has every service's
# settings):
# SLT_PG_HOST=db.example.com
# SLT_PG_PORT=5432
# SLT_PG_DB=
# SLT_PG_ADMIN_USER=
# SLT_PG_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# SLT_PG_SOURCE_USER=
# SLT_PG_SOURCE_PASSWORD=
# SLT_PG_TARGET_USER=
# SLT_PG_TARGET_PASSWORD=
# If Striim reaches it under another name than this machine does:
# SLT_POSTGRES_VIEW_HOST=
# The live Postgres container defaults to a 4g memory ceiling for parallel runs.
# Override it to suit the host's available capacity:
# SLT_POSTGRES_MEM_LIMIT=4g
